@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito66-nouns`
IMPORT `ito66-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito66-a-separate-calculation`
IMPORT `ito66-b-property-income`

-- ===========================================================================
-- SUBSECTIONS (a) AND (b) TOGETHER: whose assessment each part of the
-- spouses' taxable income falls into.
--
-- No sentence of s 66 says this in one place; it is what (a)(1), (a)(2),
-- (a)(3) and (b) say jointly, assembled.  Each figure below is a sum of
-- terms, and each term is a rule of the (a) or (b) module, cited there.
--
-- ARM ORDER.  "על אף האמור בסעיף 65" (line 2455): where a separate
-- calculation is made under (a), the (a) arm is taken and s 65 is displaced
-- to the extent (a) says.  Otherwise s 65 governs, and this row does not
-- compute what s 65 does (it is outside the slice); it reports only what (b)
-- takes out of s 65's reach, since (b) also overrides s 65.
--
-- What "assessed on the registered spouse" holds under (a): his own income
-- from personal exertion; any income from personal exertion of the other
-- spouse that the (a)(1) proviso keeps out of the separate calculation (left
-- where s 65 puts it); the pooled income not from personal exertion, if
-- (a)(2) sends it to him; and the (a)(3) income of his children under 18.
-- What the separate calculation holds: the other spouse's income from
-- personal exertion within (a)(1); the pooled income, if (a)(2) sends it to
-- her; and her (b) property income, if she claims, under the (b) proviso.
-- (The pronouns are illustrative; either spouse may be of either sex.)
--
-- The pooled income of (a)(2) is each spouse's income not from personal
-- exertion, together with any (b) property income that spouse has not
-- claimed to have calculated separately.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 66(a) and (b) — the taxable income in each calculation`

DECLARE `The calculations under subsections (a) and (b)` IS ONE OF
    `subsection (a) does not apply, and section 65 governs save for subsection (b)` HAS
        `under section 65, the registered spouse's property income calculated on its own` IS A NUMBER
        `under section 65, the other spouse's property income calculated on its own`      IS A NUMBER
    `a separate calculation is made under subsection (a)` HAS
        `taxable income assessed on the registered spouse`                IS A NUMBER
        `taxable income in the separate calculation`                       IS A NUMBER
        `the registered spouse's property income calculated on its own`   IS A NUMBER

@ref s 66(b), line 2459
GIVEN which  IS A `Which spouse`
      couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
      `where it goes` IS A `Where the property income in subsection (b) goes`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the property income of the` which `in` couple `that` `where it goes` MEANS
    IF   `s 66(b) — for` couple `, the property income goes:` which EQUALS `where it goes`
    THEN `s 66(b) — the property income of` (`the particulars of the` which `in` couple)
    ELSE 0

@ref s 66(a)(2), line 2457; s 66(b), line 2459
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(a)(2) — the taxable income not from personal exertion of the spouses, for` couple MEANS
         couple's `the registered spouse`'s `taxable income not from personal exertion`
    PLUS couple's `the spouse who is not the registered spouse`'s `taxable income not from personal exertion`
    PLUS `the property income of the` `registered spouse` `in` couple `that` `it is not calculated separately`
    PLUS `the property income of the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` couple `that` `it is not calculated separately`

-- Version 0.4.0: two terms, each 0 under the readings of 0.1.0-0.3.0: the
-- income from a failing common source that (a)(1) leaves out under reading
-- (ii) of fork F1, and the registered spouse's (b) income joined to his own
-- calculation under reading (ii) of fork F7.
@ref s 66(a)(1)-(3), lines 2456-2458; s 66(b), proviso, line 2459; s 65, line 2448; forks F1, F7
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(a) — the income assessed on the registered spouse apart from the pooled income, for` couple MEANS
         `the taxable income from personal exertion of` (couple's `the registered spouse`)
    PLUS `s 66(a)(1) — the income from personal exertion that may not be calculated separately, of` (couple's `the spouse who is not the registered spouse`)
    PLUS `s 66(a)(1) with (d)(1) — the income from a failing common source kept out of the separate calculation, for` couple
    PLUS `s 66(a)(3) — the children's income deemed the registered spouse's, for` couple
    PLUS `the property income of the` `registered spouse` `in` couple `that` `it is added to the spouse's other income for which a separate calculation is made`

-- Version 0.4.0: less the income from a failing common source kept out under
-- reading (ii) of fork F1 (0 otherwise).
@ref s 66(a)(1), line 2456; s 66(b), proviso, line 2459; fork F1
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(a) — the income in the separate calculation apart from the pooled income, for` couple MEANS
         `s 66(a)(1) — the income from personal exertion that may be calculated separately, of` (couple's `the spouse who is not the registered spouse`)
    MINUS `s 66(a)(1) with (d)(1) — the income from a failing common source kept out of the separate calculation, for` couple
    PLUS `the property income of the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` couple `that` `it is added to the spouse's other income for which a separate calculation is made`

-- The (a)(2) destination is matched FIRST, so that a couple whose incomes
-- from personal exertion are equal gets the refusal as the answer, not a
-- record holding it.
@ref s 66(a), (b), lines 2455-2459
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A `The calculations under subsections (a) and (b)`
`s 66(a)-(b) — the calculations, for` couple MEANS
    `in tax year` (couple's `tax year`) `, the answer is`
        (IF   `s 66(a)(1) — a separate calculation is made, for` couple
         THEN CONSIDER `s 66(a)(2) — the spouse to whose taxable income the income not from personal exertion is added, for` couple
              WHEN `registered spouse`
              THEN `a separate calculation is made under subsection (a)`
                      (`registered, apart from the pool` PLUS `the pool`)
                      `separate, apart from the pool`
                      `registered spouse's own (b) calculation`
              WHEN `spouse who is not the registered spouse`
              THEN `a separate calculation is made under subsection (a)`
                      (`registered, apart from the pool` MINUS `the children's income that goes with the pool`)
                      (`separate, apart from the pool` PLUS `the pool` PLUS `the children's income that goes with the pool`)
                      `registered spouse's own (b) calculation`
         ELSE `subsection (a) does not apply, and section 65 governs save for subsection (b)`
                  `registered spouse's own (b) calculation`
                  (`the property income of the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` couple `that` `it is calculated separately on its own`))
    WHERE
        `the pool`                         MEANS `s 66(a)(2) — the taxable income not from personal exertion of the spouses, for` couple
        `registered, apart from the pool`  MEANS `s 66(a) — the income assessed on the registered spouse apart from the pooled income, for` couple
        `separate, apart from the pool`    MEANS `s 66(a) — the income in the separate calculation apart from the pooled income, for` couple
        `registered spouse's own (b) calculation` MEANS
            `the property income of the` `registered spouse` `in` couple `that` `it is calculated separately on its own`
        -- Version 0.4.0, fork F14: 0 under the reading of 0.1.0-0.3.0.
        `the children's income that goes with the pool` MEANS
            `s 66(a)(2)-(3) — the children's income that goes with the pool to the spouse who is not the registered spouse, for` couple
